Proposal: Devin-Assisted PySpark Data Reliability & Ticket-to-PR Autopilot
Executive summary

The biggest recurring pain in data engineering is unplanned pipeline breakage (schema drift, upstream quirks, flaky tests) that creates downstream data debt for risk, finance, and reporting. I propose a PySpark-first solution where Devin acts as a governed, human-in-the-loop teammate that (1) hardens data quality and tests end-to-end, (2) triages & proposes fixes when pipelines fail, and (3) turns tickets → tested PRs with full audit artifacts—without direct prod write, and always behind approval gates.

Why now: GenAI’s largest value buckets include software development and content synthesis. Devin recently showed state-of-the-art, test-verified performance on SWE-bench (end-to-end GitHub issues), and enterprises are operationalizing coding agents to compress lead time and incidents—exactly where data engineering & QA spend time. 
